WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.367
-Jimmy, I love you so much.
Hi, guys.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:04.167
-John Stamos in the house.

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:05.334
-Can I start by saying --

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:08.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:10.834
Can I just say
I love you so much?

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:12.367
You bring so much.
You probably --

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:15.133
You need to hear this. You bring
so much joy to this world.

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:17.100
You make people so happy,
especially me.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.133
So God bless you. And thank you.
-Thank you.

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:22.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Isn't he the best?

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:23.734
I compare you to, like,
the greats,

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:26.367
like Sinatra,
Sammy Davis, Elvis.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:28.367
You commit 100%
to everything you do,

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:31.801
every show, every segment,
every game show you do.

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:33.267
-I was going to say
the same about you,

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.868
but now it's going to seem fake.
-It'd be weird, yeah.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.601
-But I really loved
working with you

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:39.033
on "That's My Jam."
-That was great.

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:41.367
-I will get into all of that.
I want to talk about the memoir.

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:43.267
-Sure.
-"If You Would Have Told Me."

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:45.734
-Yes.
-"If You Would Have Told Me."

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.734
Is it about "if you would have
told me that I would be --"

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:49.701
-I'd be here
with Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:50.868
I never would have believed it.

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:52.868
Seriously.
-Am I in the book?

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:54.701
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:55.868
-Now you have to add it.

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:58.801
-I talk about
losing my virginity.

00:00:58.801 --> 00:00:59.934
Oh, you know what?
-Save it for that.

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:01.300
-No. You know what's
interesting?

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.767
My mother-in-law,
who I love, you know,

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:06.834
and she's been in education
for 30 years.

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:08.868
She's got a degree
in journalism.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:09.934
I said, "Well,
take a look at the first

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:11.300
three chapters for me,
will you?"

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.033
"Okay. Okay." And I told
Caitlin, my wife,

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:14.400
and she said, "No!"

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.133
I go, "What?" She goes,
"At the end of chapter three,

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:20.234
you talk about losing
your virginity...graphically."

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:22.033
I'm like, "Oh, God."
-Oh, my God!

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:24.267
-And so I called her
and I said, "Hi, Leilani."

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:25.267
-"How far are you in the book?"

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:27.701
-Well, exactly. Yeah.
I said hi.

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:30.501
She said, "Hello, John."
So I was like, "Oh, God."

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:32.701
I said, "You know,
the end of that chapter --"

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:35.033
"Yes. You know, you're married
to my daughter. I know."

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:36.100
-Oh, my God.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.467
-She said, "You know,
my grandson."

00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:39.501
"I know, I know.
Listen, I'm sorry.

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:41.367
They wanted me to put
some sex stuff in there.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.767
And it's throughout the book."
And she says,

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.734
"What?
Oh, no, you're John Stamos.

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:45.801
Of course you're going
to talk about sex.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:47.234
Your grammar is terrible."

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:48.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:51.434
-That's a teacher right there.
That's a good teacher.

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:52.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:55.300
That is exactly right.
Get your head out of the gutter.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.167
Your grammar is terrible.
-Exactly.

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:59.767
-You know, I can't help
but think about

00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:03.234
but who would have laughed
at that is our pal Bob Saget,

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:05.133
who just had an unbelievable
sense of humor.

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:08.234
And I'm sure he's a big part
of this book.

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:10.067
-He is, yeah. I talk about him
in the beginning

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:11.534
and sort of all the way through,

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:14.133
and you were so kind to send me
a nice note when he passed away.

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:17.033
You know, I just feel awful that
he didn't know how loved he was

00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:19.801
because the world --
When he died,

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:22.200
could you believe that tsunami
of love that came out?

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.834
It was the first time
I was ever jealous of him.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:26.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:28.000
I'm kidding.
It just breaks my heart

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.300
that he didn't know
because he didn't.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.467
But he never left anything
on the table. You know that.

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:34.901
And so if he loved you, he said,

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:36.067
"I love you
and I'm proud of you."

00:02:36.067 --> 00:02:38.267
So let's keep
his legacy alive by doing --

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.634
If you're with somebody, say,
"I love you, I'm proud of you.

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:41.601
God bless you,"
that kind of thing.

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:42.834
-Yeah, why not?
Everyone do that.

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:44.067
Just look
at each other and say it.

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:45.634
-I love you.
-Say it as much as you can.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:47.133
I love you.
-I love you.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:50.033
-I love you, Roots.
-I love Quest the best.

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:54.801
-Yeah. Here's you, by the way,
at the drum set here.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:57.367
Because you play -- You
performed with The Beach Boys.

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:59.100
-Yes.
-This is a big --

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.334
That's amazing.
-It's the thrill of my life.

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:03.133
-And then look at this thrill
of your life right here.

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:04.467
-Yeah.
-How old is Billy?

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:06.467
-He's going to be five
next week.

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:09.067
And that's just one other kid
upstaging me in my life.

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:10.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:11.901
Right?
-Is it the best thing?

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:13.601
-It's the best.
You have two daughters.

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:16.300
How old are they?
-Nine and eight.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.334
-I saw them on the show
quite a bit, on your show.

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:20.367
-They didn't know that
they were on the show.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.300
It was COVID time. They didn't
even know what was happening.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.367
They thought
it was on the phone.

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:24.901
They didn't know
we were airing anything.

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:27.701
So I think they would be shy if
I brought them out or anything.

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:29.467
-They're so cute.

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:32.200
Yeah, he doesn't like and I say,
"Do you want to watch?"

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.167
"That's My Jam." I said,
"Oh." Finally I thought,

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.300
"He's going to like that show"
because he watches "Full House,"

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.133
but he mocks me for it.

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:39.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:42.267
It's like, "You know, Billy,
can you put your toys away?"

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:43.834
He'd go, "You got it, dude."

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:45.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:47.501
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.033
-I love this kid!

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:51.234
[ Applause ]

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:52.634
I love this kid.

00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:54.634
-So I thought he would
really like "That's My Jam."

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:57.133
So we put it on and he watches
and goes, "You're cheating."

00:03:57.133 --> 00:03:59.234
I'm like, "I'm not cheating."

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:00.868
-Yeah, you were.
-I was not.

00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:01.901
-Yeah, you were.
-No, I wasn't.

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:03.400
-Yeah, he's right.
-What?

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.734
-You cheated.
-No, I didn't.

00:04:04.734 --> 00:04:05.667
-Yeah.
-I did?

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:07.167
-Yeah.
-Where?

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:08.701
-I actually have a picture
of you cheating.

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:10.100
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.033
-Well, this is where --
-Let's see.

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:14.267
-Well, the idea of the game
is someone's doing charades

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:15.801
while the wall spins around,

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:17.734
so you're not supposed to see
what they're seeing.

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:19.501
But here's you actually
peeking around the wall

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:22.434
and cheating.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.434 --> 00:04:23.868
You're not supposed to do that.

00:04:23.868 --> 00:04:27.801
You were so funny and charming
and talented on this show.

00:04:27.801 --> 00:04:29.133
Can I just say this?

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:31.667
You can plug your ears
about this, but man, oh, man,

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:34.434
it was charming.
Yeah. Everything I just said.

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:37.601
You did this one game
where we had random instruments

00:04:37.601 --> 00:04:40.033
and you had to pick up
and you had to try to play out

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:42.934
the note of a song or somehow
get someone to guess the song.

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:44.767
-Right.
-And we don't rig it.

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:46.801
You don't know what songs
you're getting or anything.

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:48.868
You picked up this, like, bass
ukulele or something.

00:04:48.868 --> 00:04:49.868
-I don't know what that was.
-And played

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:51.400
"Play That Funky Music
White Boy"

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.868
and you picked up
and you're like, "Boom, boom,

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:55.434
ba boom, ba boom, boom, boom,
boom, boom, boom, boom, boom.

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:57.634
I was like, professionally.
-Yeah.

00:04:57.634 --> 00:04:59.501
-People went nuts,
-Quinta said

00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:01.901
he's actually a white
boy playing that funky music.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:05.634
-It actually did happen. White
boy was playing that --

00:05:05.634 --> 00:05:06.634
-Thank you for
having me on that show.

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:07.901
It was so fun.

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:09.367
-The whole band
was looking like,

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:10.801
"Yo, this guy could play, man."

00:05:10.801 --> 00:05:12.367
-And we won.
I was happy to be nominated,

00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:14.300
but we won.
-Yeah. Exactly.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:18.601
You did win.
You and Taraji, winning team.

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:22.501
Buddy, I will do anything
with you

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:25.033
and any idea you come up with
or anything.

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:27.067
-Really? Okay.
-I love you.

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:28.968
-I love you, too.
I really do.

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:31.400
I've just been such a big fan of
you for so long.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:32.801
-But every time you come
on the show,

00:05:32.801 --> 00:05:35.200
you've done bits with Bob.
You've done bits by yourself.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.834
And "That's My Jam."
If you honestly --

00:05:36.834 --> 00:05:38.033
-What about that song
I sang on there?

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.601
Will you do that with me?

00:05:39.601 --> 00:05:43.200
They had me doing
weird lyrics to "YMCA,"

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:46.767
but it was like I shared
an Uber with Tim Chalamet.

00:05:46.767 --> 00:05:48.701
-Yeah.
-Which you'll get it stuck --

00:05:48.701 --> 00:05:51.000
It's an earwig and my wife has
been singing it in bed, which...

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.200
-♪ I took an Uber with ♪

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.200
♪ Tim Chalamet ♪

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:58.667
♪ Not the actor, just some guy
from L.A. ♪

00:05:58.667 --> 00:06:01.267
-Again, you don't know what
those lyrics are going to be.

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:03.234
So you're reading the
teleprompter for the first time.

00:06:03.234 --> 00:06:04.868
We actually have a clip.

00:06:04.868 --> 00:06:07.767
Here's John Stamos
singing nonsense karaoke

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:09.634
on "That's My Jam."
Take a look at this.

00:06:09.634 --> 00:06:11.067
-♪ Plump hands ♪

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:13.067
♪ Can't wear gloves
when it snows ♪

00:06:13.067 --> 00:06:14.968
♪ I watch C-Span ♪

00:06:14.968 --> 00:06:17.033
♪ With a grape up my nose ♪

00:06:17.033 --> 00:06:18.801
♪ My ex-girlfriend ♪

00:06:18.801 --> 00:06:20.901
♪ Looks like Optimus Prime ♪

00:06:20.901 --> 00:06:25.467
♪ Hold on, Craig...wants...me
to...FaceTime ♪

00:06:25.467 --> 00:06:27.667
Can't right now, Craig.
Here we go.

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:29.367
♪ I split an Uber with ♪

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:31.701
♪ Tim Chalamet ♪

00:06:31.701 --> 00:06:35.534
♪ Not the actor,
just some guy from L.A. ♪

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:38.467
I can't get that out of my mind.

00:06:38.467 --> 00:06:39.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
-We're wearing beards.

00:06:39.968 --> 00:06:42.100
You look good with a beard.
-You too.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:44.901
-That's for a movie, right?
-It was. Yeah.

00:06:44.901 --> 00:06:46.300
-When that movie comes out,
please come back.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:47.767
-I would love to. Thank you.
-You are more than welcome.

00:06:47.767 --> 00:06:49.267
We love you every
single -- You come --

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:50.767
Don't even leave.
Stay the whole week.

00:06:50.767 --> 00:06:52.667
It's John Stamos Week
here on "The Tonight Show."

00:06:52.667 --> 00:06:54.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:54.634 --> 00:06:58.033
Check out "That's My Jam" but
also preorder his memoir,

00:06:58.033 --> 00:07:00.801
"If You Would Have Told Me."
Preorder it right now.

